  "slug": "uncertainty-topic-be90",
  "summary": "Seven preprints tighten certification and bounds for entanglement, nonstabilizerness, nonlocality, channel capacity, and pseudorandom unitary security.",
  "synthesis": "The items converge on quantifying and certifying quantum resources under constrained access. Scrambling is tied to entanglement cost in non-local quantum computation, with tripartite mutual information as a faithful witness. Magic is certified via a stabilizer pigeonhole criterion and worst-case random access codes, while a separate work shows the stabilizer norm of the Choi state does not fully fix Pauli-limited channel certification robustness once positivity is imposed. Nonlocal extremal behaviours in Q2222 receive explicit normal cones with device-independent applications. Cryptographic and information-theoretic limits also tighten: birthday-scale non-adaptive security of the DPFC strong pseudorandom unitary, with adaptive security failing; an entanglement attack on quantum differential privacy and an entanglement-assisted remedy; and an amplitude-damping two-way capacity bound tighter than PLOB.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
